Task: Axis-aligned non-solid box hitboxes (FR5) — Phase 2, task 1

Summary of changes:
- collectObstacles now maps every prop to exactly one shape: a circle when the
  grid publishes a collision radius, and otherwise the footprint BOX the grid
  already turned by the car's yaw, solid: false. Before this, a prop with no
  radius was dropped from the list entirely, so a parked car had no hitbox at
  all and could be driven through without a bonk — the comment claiming they
  were "boxed by its footprint instead" described intent, not code.
- A prop that offers neither a radius nor a footprint now throws instead of
  being skipped: a prop nobody can hit is a prop the car drives through, which
  is exactly the bug this task fixes.
- vehicleMotor's spring-back now clears SOLID hitboxes. Driving the pose the new
  tests describe found this: a bonk whose normal points at a wall springs the
  car into it, because a parked car leaves only 0.037 to the house behind it
  while the recoil travels 0.14. The clamp applies to solids alone, since
  driving over a bumped crashable is the designed outcome.
- Coverage: the "marks buildings solid and props crashable" assertion was
  updated to the new contract (every prop is crashable; parked cars differ in
  shape, not in what a bonk costs the route).

Files created: none.
Files modified:
- src/game/collision/collision.ts (+ its test: 7 new tests)
- src/game/vehicle/vehicleMotor.ts (+ its test: 4 new tests)
- src/game/town/townGrid.test.ts (a diagonal parked yaw must fail at map load)

Why:
A parked car has to be something the car can bonk, but the shape matters as much
as the presence: a circle big enough to cover its 0.55 length reaches 0.185 from
the street centre line, inside the player's own 0.26 capsule, so it would bonk
every centre-line drive — the exact thing FR4 forbids. Tests assert the contrast
in both directions: the box passes the centre-line sweep that the covering
circle fails, and the leg still completes where the same car made solid would
strand it at the kerb.

